KI-cLoop: Closing the reaction-to-process loop with knowledge-intensified AI

Parts of the knowledge-retrieval code derive from BaranziniLab/KG_RAG,
"Biomedical knowledge graph-enhanced prompt generation for large language
models", distributed under the Apache License 2.0.

Project-specific components include reaction and material retrieval,
hybrid PINN-ODE kinetic inference, experimental data processing, evaluation,
screening, environmental accounting and knowledge-reuse analyses.

Source-derived retrieval records are attributed in
knowledge/data/application_route_sources.jsonl. External scientific databases,
model weights and provider APIs retain their respective licenses and terms.
Full source datasets and model weights are obtained separately.
